# Backend Project Structure Rules

- Keep routing, service/use-case logic, schemas/models, and data-access code in separate modules.
- Do not place heavy business logic directly inside route handlers.
- Group code by domain feature where possible to reduce cross-module coupling.
- Keep shared utilities small and generic; avoid turning utils into a catch-all module.
- Co-locate tests with the corresponding domain area under `tests/`.
- Split files when they become hard to scan or mix unrelated responsibilities.

## Example
```python
# routers/leads.py -> HTTP layer
# services/leads.py -> business logic
# repositories/leads.py -> persistence logic
```
